      "content": "To determine how many questions Frank answered correctly, let's define the variables and set up the equations based on the given information.\n\nLet:\n- \\( x \\) be the number of questions Frank answered correctly.\n- \\( y \\) be the number of questions Frank answered incorrectly.\n\nFrom the problem, we know the following:\n1. Frank answered a total of 80 questions.\n2. Frank scored 232 points.\n3. Each correct answer is worth 5 points.\n4. Each incorrect answer is worth -2 points.\n5. Each question not answered is worth 0 points.\n\nWe can set up the following system of equations based on the information given:\n\n1. \\( x + y = 80 \\) (since Frank answered a total of 80 questions)\n2. \\( 5x - 2y = 232 \\) (since each correct answer scores 5 points and each incorrect answer scores -2 points)\n\nFirst, solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 80 - x\n\\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( y = 80 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\n\\[\n5x - 2(80 - x) = 232\n\\]\n\nSimplify and solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n5x - 160 + 2x = 232\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n7x - 160 = 232\n\\]\n\nAdd 160 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n7x = 392\n\\]\n\nDivide by 7:\n\n\\[\nx = 56\n\\]\n\nSo, Frank answered \\( x = 56 \\) questions correctly. To verify, we can find \\( y \\):\n\n\\[\ny = 80 - x = 80 - 56 = 24\n\\]\n\nNow, check the score calculation:\n\n\\[\n5x - 2y = 5(56) - 2(24) = 280 - 48 = 232\n\\]\n\nThe calculations confirm the score is correct. Therefore, the number of questions Frank answered correctly is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{56}\n\\]"
